{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/176759-any-updated-information-on-scion-origins","id":176759,"title":"Any updated information on Scion:Origins?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","Scion"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-06-21T22:58:18-07:00","id":176759,"title":"<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/icons/icon5.png\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" alt=\"\" /> Any updated information on Scion:Origins?","content":"I haven't heard anything new about it yet other than it is supposedly going to be out in August.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1246-arthurhansen","name":"ArthurHansen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1246_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"66"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-21T23:07:36-07:00","id":176767,"title":"","content":"That's unlikely, at this point, given the system's currently being compiled and they've just got the first character piece in.<br /> <br /> This page compiles what we currently know about 2e: <a href=\"http://www.ttrarchive.com/store/index.php?title=Scion_2E:_What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.ttrarchive.com/store/inde...:_What_We_Know</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-22T17:02:45-07:00","id":177458,"title":"","content":"It's 5 out of 7 steps along (according to the release page) and supposed to be released in August. August, of course, is not that far away any more.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1246-arthurhansen","name":"ArthurHansen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1246_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"66"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-22T23:49:55-07:00","id":177718,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArthurHansen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/176759-any-updated-information-on-scion-origins?p=177458#post177458\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's 5 out of 7 steps along (according to the release page) and supposed to be released in August. August, of course, is not that far away any more.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's for Book of the Wyrm, the book above it. Look at the progress bar below the Origins entry, which is at 1 step out of 7.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-23T05:07:28-07:00","id":177838,"title":"","content":"Speaking for myself of course, I would not see this project too rushed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-24T13:37:27-07:00","id":179203,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadowflame</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/176759-any-updated-information-on-scion-origins?p=177838#post177838\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Speaking for myself of course, I would not see this project too rushed.</div> </div> </div> </div>Agreed. I'm watching the Exalted 3rd Edition development, and that's been very slow indeed. Granted, they're playtesting things right now to build a solid base for what I might consider a broader final scope of what can be played (That is, a Dragon-Blood or Sidereal plays and handles and generally operates much more differently from a Solar than, say, a Scion of the Dodekatheon does from the Aesir.) But I honestly expect the Scion system development to take longer: whereas the Exalted 3e System is a tweaked Storyteller mechanic, I'm gathering that the mechanics at the heart of Scion and Trinity's system are going to be more removed, and probably shall require more development.<br /> <br /> Regardless, I'm still waiting with great anticipation for this, and have every intention of snapping it up the moment it comes out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/561-mockery","name":"Mockery","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar561_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"876"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-24T23:50:09-07:00","id":179498,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mockery</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/176759-any-updated-information-on-scion-origins?p=179203#post179203\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Agreed. I'm watching the Exalted 3rd Edition development, and that's been very slow indeed. Granted, they're playtesting things right now to build a solid base for what I might consider a broader final scope of what can be played (That is, a Dragon-Blood or Sidereal plays and handles and generally operates much more differently from a Solar than, say, a Scion of the Dodekatheon does from the Aesir.) But I honestly expect the Scion system development to take longer: whereas the Exalted 3e System is a tweaked Storyteller mechanic, I'm gathering that the mechanics at the heart of Scion and Trinity's system are going to be more removed, and probably shall require more development.<br /> <br /> Regardless, I'm still waiting with great anticipation for this, and have every intention of snapping it up the moment it comes out.</div> </div> </div> </div>Mm.<br /> <br /> I very much get the idea they were expecting to have the basic system compiled and out to public examination by now, but writing it up and pulling everything together - I assume that's what compiling means - is taking longer than expected.<br /> <br /> After public examination would probably come modifying the system for the particular game, as Scion and Trinity's requirements are different.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-25T06:04:17-07:00","id":179612,"title":"","content":"As a person that doesn't even play the game, I'm not big on the mechanics. To me it's how the ideas in such a book are presented. And that means writing ability. I've bought every Palladium's books on Rifts and plenty of other lines for no other reason than ideas and how well written they are. (The whole &quot;Seige on Tolkeen&quot; series was amazing to me, and could have just as easily been a novelization that would have read just as well. It was that good.)<br /> Although I realize that things are different, I haven't felt disappointed yet in the existing books. So I'm still sure that the books are going to be well-written. But I know that it takes some time.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":144,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","user":"Shadowflame","date":".  qualifier 06-25-2014, 09:05 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-25T10:30:22-07:00","id":179839,"title":"","content":"Those of us who <i>do</i> play Scion are very fervently hoping for functional mechanics. That's what basically killed Scion's First Edition and made it one of the least played games released by White Wolf. The IDEAS were great, but the system was terribly, terribly broken and entirely non-functional past the first tier.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm a professor! Why is no one listening to me?!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/235-telgar","name":"Telgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar235_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-25T16:14:15-07:00","id":180147,"title":"","content":"Telgar- Your remark &quot;one of the least played games released by WW&quot; is simply untrue. Every release for Scion did very well, far beyond any reasonable idea that they were all bought just to read- people played. For many it wasn't easy, for some it was, and for others it was impossible because of the rules.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5-richt","name":"RichT","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5_2.jpeg","title":"Onyx Path Creative Director","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-29T06:38:45-07:00","id":183735,"title":"","content":"These players are very mysterious and secretive then. I've never encounters another group in person that has actually played the game, and it is and always has been incredibly rare to find online groups being built for it. This contrasts with pretty much every other White Wolf line which sees widespread play. Most groups that play White Wolf games have at least tried all White Wolf lines.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/151-hark","name":"Hark","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar151_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"932"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-29T08:45:13-07:00","id":183845,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hark</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/176759-any-updated-information-on-scion-origins?p=183735#post183735\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">These players are very mysterious and secretive then. I've never encounters another group in person that has actually played the game, and it is and always has been incredibly rare to find online groups being built for it. This contrasts with pretty much every other White Wolf line which sees widespread play. Most groups that play White Wolf games have at least tried all White Wolf lines.</div> </div> </div> </div>I've found that most of the online Scion games are pulled from existing groups who already know each other and are rarely advertised on the forums themselves because, let's face it, Scion was quiet before and with Hero's Journey a thing now, the Scion forums are basically dead (until the new edition, hopefully).<br /> <br /> I think a lot of it has to do with the need for RAW Scion to be houseruled so much; it's easier to stick with groups who all have the same vision rather than hope you pick up a good apple on the forums as a pick-up.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/606-aynie","name":"Aynie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar606_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-29T09:20:09-07:00","id":183860,"title":"","content":"Another reason you tend reason why there are not a lot of people recruiting for online games is that that some of the members on the this and the old forums tend to so set on how see the game they can't deal with how others see the game - and after so many failed recruitment threads I know I've just given up trying I assume it like that for others as well","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/324-ardenty","name":"ardenty","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar324_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"45"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-29T17:27:20-07:00","id":184230,"title":"","content":"I have run 3 different campaigns for Scion and all were extremely fun (about to do a 4th)! There was a major problem with the rules, but you just had to work around them. I tend to find a rule or three I don't agree with in almost all rpgs I run. I just alter it a bit and keep on truckin. Scion, on the other hand was a bit of a mess. If you worked on it and kept a close eye on things (using Baron S's corrections was a major help) you could have a really fast paced and engrossing game. I look forward to the new system. I hope it fixes the glitches from the first and makes it a smooth to run game.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1528-hivemind","name":"Hivemind","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1528_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-03T10:21:13-07:00","id":187230,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hivemind</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/176759-any-updated-information-on-scion-origins?p=184230#post184230\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have run 3 different campaigns for Scion and all were extremely fun (about to do a 4th)! There was a major problem with the rules, but you just had to work around them. I tend to find a rule or three I don't agree with in almost all rpgs I run. I just alter it a bit and keep on truckin. Scion, on the other hand was a bit of a mess. If you worked on it and kept a close eye on things (using Baron S's corrections was a major help) you could have a really fast paced and engrossing game. I look forward to the new system. I hope it fixes the glitches from the first and makes it a smooth to run game.</div> </div> </div> </div>+1. I've run...at least two chronicles that went on for a while before either players went their separate ways, or running two games at once finally took its toll on me. And I've played in a couple games. And I've run a couple one-shots.<br /> <br /> Most of the groups I've played it with have ended up having one of the players end up saying, &quot;Hey, <i>I </i>want to run this!&quot; after we're done.<br /> <br /> On none of these occasions were house rules employed. This...was to my detriment as an ST. I'm looking forward to the next edition tightening things up.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/561-mockery","name":"Mockery","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar561_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"876"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-05T03:38:58-07:00","id":188633,"title":"","content":"On another note, in the postings in the last Monday Morning blurb, they did state that Scion: Origins will have a Kickstarter before being added to DTRPG.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/891-jackalopevegas","name":"JackalopeVegas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"246"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-05T09:19:52-07:00","id":188772,"title":"","content":"I've run 5 or so Scion games. &quot;Or so&quot; because one cycle involved largely the same group of players playing members of two Scion bands in a connected continuity. (One civilian band in American. One military band in Iraq.) Not sure if I should count that as 5 or 6 then...<br /> <br /> I've used House Rules in every one. Not the same House Rules and not all House Rules used in one game got used in the next. A lot of &quot;forum shopping&quot; to use a loosely related legal term. It was pretty obvious from the outset that some rules were just not going to cut it. For example, Jotunblut, on it's face was not useful for most players who wanted to play Aesir characters. (Though we did use it as written in the military game, where the Lt. used it on his squad to given them some extra oomph in fights...).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-05T09:42:29-07:00","id":188777,"title":"","content":"I'll definitely be at Gen Con, spilling secrets about the game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-05T09:54:37-07:00","id":188786,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JackalopeVegas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/176759-any-updated-information-on-scion-origins?p=188633#post188633\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On another note, in the postings in the last Monday Morning blurb, they did state that Scion: Origins will have a Kickstarter before being added to DTRPG.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well... not quite. They said there'll be a Scion KS, but not what'll be in it - like, will it be for both Origins and 2e Hero or for just Origins? That may be something they haven't decided yet.<br /> <br /> (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/183175-question-about-the-trin-cont-kickstarter-projects-page\">Rose Bailey's said</a> they haven't decided how to do the Trinity Continuum KS yet, and a similar thing may hold here.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":51,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","user":"marin","date":".  Correcting the source on the Continuum KS 07-05-2014, 01:01 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-05T11:39:51-07:00","id":188836,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>marin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/176759-any-updated-information-on-scion-origins?p=177718#post177718\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's for Book of the Wyrm, the book above it. Look at the progress bar below the Origins entry, which is at 1 step out of 7.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, sorry about that. Scion Hero (also August) doesn't even have a 1 of X bar.<br /> <br /> Thought without almost any supernatural powers, Scion:Origins might be pretty simple, actually. So it might not take a lot of 'rules' tweaks.<br /> <br /> Huh. Reading Percy Jackson again, there are some really neat ways that Riordan handled the flavor of things that's very 'setting' and dynamic. Like Healing is mostly a skill and/or potions. And it isn't instantaneous for the most part. It would incredibly nerf the Healing Purview... but it felt a lot more mythic and less video game healing.<br /> <br /> And the more elemental connection of powers, where you are weaker away from elements but strong actually in or next to them I like as a story, but I'm not sure you could do justice to it in a dice game.<br /> <br /> Though it feels very weird that you can't affect the weather at all really (Sky) until you are Legend 11. So you can't have you moods connect with the weather even slightly.<br /> <br /> Weather Witch is laughably short distance in a modern setting where you can fly thousands of miles in a single day in an airplane as a mortal, but you can only figure out weather within about Legend*miles distance when you use the power.<br /> <br /> Sorry for the rambling.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1246-arthurhansen","name":"ArthurHansen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1246_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"66"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-05T19:19:10-07:00","id":189054,"title":"","content":"Percy Jackson's Hades &lt; Jim Butcher's Hades<br /> <br /> Seriously, I really can't grasp the love for Percy Jackson. Poseidon was such as an intolerable cruel ass in the myths. And now he's made into this almost huggable guy?<br /> <br /> I have to wonder when Butcher wrote about Hades, he had some criticism for Riordan's series in mind.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-10T04:08:36-07:00","id":193376,"title":"","content":"Scion's been moved to &quot;On the horizon...&quot; No dates confirmed...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1837-wickedgrail","name":"Wickedgrail","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1837_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-10T16:55:54-07:00","id":194100,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wickedgrail</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/176759-any-updated-information-on-scion-origins?p=193376#post193376\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Scion's been moved to &quot;On the horizon...&quot; No dates confirmed...</div> </div> </div> </div>Very sad... Will have to hope for more info soon! I really want Scion to be done 'right' rather than just rushed though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1246-arthurhansen","name":"ArthurHansen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1246_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"66"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-11T19:04:31-07:00","id":195185,"title":"","content":"<b><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> On the horizon\u2026 </div> </div> </div></b><br /><br /><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"color:#444444\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>Scion \u2013 Scion: Origins</b>: Building on our shared love of mythology, Scion unveils a war that shakes the pillars of reality itself. Players take on the role of the children of the Gods, battling the Titanspawn and their own twisted fate. If these Scions live long enough, they\u2019ll ascend to the Overworld themselves to take their parents\u2019 place in a conflict going back to the dawn of time. Begin as a mortal. Become a God. <i>Developer: Joseph D. Carriker, Jr. PDF/PoD</i></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#444444\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"> <span style=\"color:#ECECEC\"><span style=\"font-size:30px\"> 1 of 7</span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> </span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#444444\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>Scion \u2013 Scion: Hero </b>: <i>Developer: Joseph D. Carriker, Jr. PDF/PoD</i></span></span></span> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#444444\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><i><br /> <br /> I don't think they have Scion: Hero properly shown on the list. It sort of looks like they don't have a progress bar.</i></span></span></span><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1246-arthurhansen","name":"ArthurHansen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1246_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"66"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-12T00:03:04-07:00","id":195308,"title":"","content":"I wouldn't read too much into this. Onyx Path has gotten complaints about books that are in development being kept on the list with an estimated date constantly being pushed back.<br /> <br /> So things like Scion, Exalted 3rd Edition, and so on that they don't have a real solid date on besides &quot;when it's done&quot; are put in &quot;on the horizon&quot; rather than constantly shifting the estimates out when they aren't met.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}